After a long break from NH, I picked up the game again and tried some of 
the clesses I don't usually play, tourist, knight, etc; and did better 
than I expected (one tourist finished the quest and got as far as the 
castle before dying fairly stupidly). I think the biggest reason for the 
improvement, apart from reading spoilers and r.g.r.n a bit more was 
re-discovering the great value of leaning heavily on pets in the early game.

Anyway, I thought I'd see how I did with an "easy" class. I always play 
my wizards as spell combat spell casters (not that I never hit in melee, 
of course), and this time I even switched to a robe from [CoMR once I 
got another source of MR, for the bonus casting hard spells.

I would say he had more than his fair share of luck. I had 
YA-would-be-SD (saved by "oLS) when I thought I could take out a 
cross-aligned mine town priest with a wand of death... standing inside 
the shrine. This turned out to be a triple mistake, not only did Ptah, 
smite me (blowing up the wand of death, serves me right), but the priest 
has a [CoMR and I never found another priest to buy protection from 
either. I lost a second "oLS fighting the Dark One, which is almost as 
embaresing, though I wasn't equipped well for the fight, not having 
Magicbane yet (no altars).

Thankfully the Dark One's level has an altar so I got it soon after. 
Once wizards get that and their quest artifact there isn't much that can 
stand in their way. The one thing that concerned me, was the lack of 
[SDSM. I didn't get any wishes before (or after) the castle. I reached 
the castle wearing +2 studded leather and some well enchant accessories.

Just before entering Gehenome, I did something I never have before, and 
intentionally prayed to get crowned. A +oFoD is probably the best 
crowning gift. After reaching the bottom of hell I warpped back to my 
quest area, which I had been using as a base and alchemied up my HP to 400.

Thw Rodney was no problem (I hope no one tells that guy about [CoMR). 
The high priest was  no problem. Amusingly I used the same method that 
almost got me killed in mine town, but this time I had reflection, and 
he didn't have MR.

The way up through hell was only slightly annoying, teleportation makes 
it pretty painless. I got a couple random monster summons, once a swarm 
including a coatl (sp?) while levitating over water, that was a bit 
scary, but no harm came of it. Thanks to Magicbane, the worst random 
curse was getting my (BoH unblessed once.

Before leaving the dungeon, I did the 7 sacks trick to double-(BoH my 
loot. Gratuitous, be kinda fun.

Air was the only elemental plane that felt at all threatening. Water 
tedious but so tame I thought I'd wait to let me power recharge before 
entering the portal, only to have it get away from me again. :sigh:
Finding the altar on Astral took two tries. I put r.g.r.n advice to good 
use and used jumping boots, haste self and plenty of wands of 
teleportation. The only tight spot was when I got cornered between some 
angels and priests and Death. He took a good chunk out of my max HP, I 
didn't realize he did that.

I don't have a log of his attributes and junk since I'm on the tiled 
interface for DOS and didn't think to switch to ascii before Offering 
the amulet.

Final score: 4510418.

